---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import heroImage from '@/assets/illustrations/farm-field-hero.png';
import { withBase } from '@/data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Alexander and Katherine Collamore, learn why they moved to Alaska in 2012, and discover the family influence behind the name Poor Louis Farms.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="The family and the name" title="A farm built by making things and staying curious." intro="Poor Louis Farms is a small family farm in Wasilla, run by Alexander and Katherine Collamore with the everyday company—and perspective—of their three children." number="07" />
  <section class="section--tight section--paper-light">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><Image src={heroImage} alt="Illustrated garden rows and work shed at the edge of an Alaska forest; an artistic scene rather than the actual Poor Louis Farms property." widths={[480, 768, 1120]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 92vw, 48vw" format="webp" loading="eager" /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">North since 2012</p>
        <h2>From Washington to a hands-on life in Alaska.</h2>
        <p>Alexander and Katherine moved from Washington to Alaska in 2012. Their backgrounds in design, fabrication, and practical making found new material in a place where light, weather, local plants, and a short growing season set the pace.</p>
        <p>Tea, spice blends, hot sauce, salves, flowers, home goods, and seasonal experiments may look like separate pursuits. At the worktable they are connected by the same habits: observe closely, make a small run, record what happened, and improve the next one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split split--top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Behind the name</p>
        <h2>Robert Louis Triebenbach's influence travels with the farm.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Alexander's late grandfather helped inspire his dream of becoming a farmer. The name Poor Louis Farms keeps that influence present without turning it into a grand legend.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/journal/behind-the-name/')}>Read the longer field note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="story-ledger">
        <div class="story-row"><dt>People</dt><dd>Alexander and Katherine Collamore and their three children</dd></div>
        <div class="story-row"><dt>Place</dt><dd>Wasilla, Alaska</dd></div>
        <div class="story-row"><dt>Since</dt><dd>Moved to Alaska in 2012</dd></div>
        <div class="story-row"><dt>Method</dt><dd>Grow, gather, make, test, record, revise</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--paper-light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">What guides the work</p><h2>Three ordinary, durable principles.</h2></div>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <article class="principle"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Say what is known.</h3><p>Ingredients, origins, and process details are stated precisely. Unconfirmed details are left open rather than polished into a claim.</p></article>
        <article class="principle"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Let seasons be real.</h3><p>Availability can change. A harvest window is not a marketing countdown, and an experiment does not have to become a product.</p></article>
        <article class="principle"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Keep curiosity useful.</h3><p>Experimentation matters when it improves flavor, handling, craft, or understanding—not when it merely makes the story sound unusual.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--ink"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">From story to shelf</p><h2>See what the current season has produced.</h2></div><div><p>Browse product stories here, then use Square for live availability and checkout.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button button--light" href={withBase('/products/')}>Explore products</a><a class="button" href="https://poor-louis-farms.square.site/s/shop" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shop on Square <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
